      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1904-03-26_WidnesExaminer_art0034" n="art0034">
        <head>ILL-FATED 7 SUBMARINE.</head>
        <p>THE ILL-FATED 7 SUBMARINE.</p>
        <p>it was found to be missing due significance was attached to it. Search was made, but the wreck was not located until Saturday noon. She was then found lying in deep water near the spot indicated by the Ber- wick Castle, and as she appears to have been instantly flooded after being struck, those on board must have speedily succumbed. The gallant crew, includit.g the two officers in command—Lieutenant Mansergh and Sub- Lieutenant Churchill—numbered eleven, and the deepest regret at the painful occurrence has been expressed by Sir John Fisher, the Commander-in-Chief at Portsmouth.</p>
