        <p>provision for their confort should cammunicate with Mr. Harry Ashton, Bridge Foot. Bradford played Leigh at Bradford on Tuesday and whacked the Mather Laners by 17 points to 5 points, thus taking the lead in the League. The Northern Rugby League Committee on Tuesday night decided to play the postponed international match at Wigan on Easter Tuesday. It was also resolved that the international teams be re-arranged, and that four three-quarters be played instead of three. In the English team J. Lomas (Salford), was chosen as fourth three-quarter, and G. H. Marsden (Bradford) as half- back. The Other Nationalities team will include D. Harris (Wigan) and T. D. Llewellyn (Leeds) as centres and Sam James and William James (Broughton Rangers) as half-backs. The Works Competition commenced last evening, when the Cable Co. defeated the Locos by 5 paints to three.</p>
